    "statement": "Write the number of the correct choice. \nTwo bus tickets from city A to B and three tickets from city A to C cost Rs. 77 but three tickets from city \nA to B and two tickets from city A to C cost Rs. 73. What are the fares for cities B and C from A?",
    "type": "single_choice",
    "images": [],
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "text": "Rs. 4, Rs. 23"
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "text": "Rs. 13, Rs. 17"
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "text": "Rs. 15, Rs. 14"
      },
      {
        "id": "4",
        "text": "Rs. 17, Rs. 13"
      }
    ],
    "dropdownGroups": [],
    "correctAnswer": "(2)",
    "explanation": "Let Rs. x be the fare of city B from city A and Rs. y be the fare of city C from city A.\nThen, 2x + 3y = 77 ...(i) and\n3x + 2y = 73 ...(ii)\nMultiplying (i) by 3 and (ii) by 2 and subtracting, we get: 5y = 85 or y = 17.\nPutting y = 17 in (i), we get: x = 13.",
    "solutionImages": [],
    "pdfPage": 261
